# 220 to 225: the files.
{220}{}{VISITORS. "Man in a blue jumpsuit, yellow number on his back. Asked after a Vault and a garden in a box. Told him nothing, for forty dollars. He went east, to Vault City. Vault folk, high walls. Next one who asks pays a hundred."}
{221}{}{SIMMS, L. "Pays his tab. Cannot be bought; tried twice. Soft spots: the boy, and the bomb. Would hand the empty house by the gate to whoever made the thing safe. I'd have sold the same favor for less."}
{222}{}{BURKE. "Came alone, no dust on his shoes. Pays in pre-War money, crisp. Asks about the bomb the way other men ask about women. Whoever sent him has more where that came from. Do not cross. Do overcharge."}
{223}{}{STAHL, L. "Buys more chems than one man needs and fewer than one man sells. Thinks nobody knows. Good for one large favor from the Brass Lantern, on the day I want one."}
{224}{}{WATER PLANT. "Three pipes split and counting. The town pays two hundred to whoever stops them. Walter buys scrap metal besides, twenty-five apiece. Have Gob save the bottle caps. No. Worthless."}
{225}{}{WAGES. "Gob: owed, fifteen years. Nova: owed, three. Held in trust, strongbox, by my bed, where I can hear it. A hundred and eighty in hand. The interest accrues to the house."}
